---
import Layout from "../../layouts/Layout.astro";
---

<Layout title="Just Capture Privacy Policy">
    <h1>Just Capture Privacy Policy</h1>
    <p>
        <em>Last updated: November 5, 2026</em>
    </p>

    <p>
        Just Capture ("the App") is an iPhone and Android app published by Just
        Free Software, Inc. ("we", "us"). It records video, tries to upload it to
        your own Google Drive, and can email the people you choose when you start
        recording. This policy covers both versions of the App. Where they differ,
        we say so.
    </p>

    <h2>Summary</h2>
    <ul>
        <li>
            We don't operate servers for the App. Your videos, location, email
            recipients, and account details are never sent to us.
        </li>
        <li>
            Your videos are stored on your phone and in your own Google Drive.
        </li>
        <li>
            <strong>
                If the App emails people about a recording, it sets that
                recording's Drive folder to "Anyone with the link".
            </strong>{" "}
            Anyone who has the link can view the recording and, if "Save location"
            is on, a trail of where you were during it. Otherwise, the folder stays private.
        </li>
        <li>
            The App has no analytics or advertising SDKs, and we don't sell your
            data.
        </li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Information We Collect</h2>
    <p>
        We don't collect personal information through the App, and the App has no
        Just Capture account. The information below is handled on your device and
        by the services you connect the App to.
    </p>
    <p>
        If you email us, we receive your email address and whatever you include
        in your message, and we use it to respond to you.
    </p>
    <p>
        If you've chosen to share analytics with app developers on your iPhone,
        Apple may give us crash reports and usage statistics. Apple presents this
        data to developers in aggregated or de-identified form. On Android, Google
        Play may similarly give us crash reports and usage statistics, depending
        on your device's settings.
    </p>

    <h2>Camera and Microphone</h2>
    <p>
        The App uses your camera and microphone to record video with sound. It
        records only after you start a recording. Recordings may capture other
        people and your surroundings. You are responsible for following the laws
        where you record.
    </p>

    <h2>Location</h2>
    <p>
        The App uses your location to keep a record of where you were during each
        recording and to include your starting location in notification emails. It
        asks for permission to use your location while the App is in use, and you
        can deny this and still record.
    </p>
    <p>
        You control this with "Save location" in Settings, which is on by default.
        With it off, the App doesn't get your location, even if you've given
        permission. With it on, the App gets your location when it opens or you
        grant permission, and continuously for as long as you're recording, whether
        or not you've set up email notifications. To look up an address, it sends
        coordinates about once a minute at most while recording: on iPhone, to
        Apple's maps service, and on Android, to your device's geocoding service,
        which is usually provided by Google. If a location is rough, the App shows
        only the general area.
</p>
    <p>
        The App saves a trail of your location for each recording: one point when
        you start recording and one when each clip ends, with the time, coordinates,
        and accuracy of each point. If your current location isn't available when a
        clip ends, the trail uses and labels your last known location, or notes that
        none is available. The trail is saved on your device and
uploaded as a file called <code>location.txt</code> to the recording's
        Google Drive folder, where it's updated as you record. <strong>If that
        folder is shared by link, anyone with the link can see your trail, including
        while you're still recording.</strong> If you've set up notifications, emails
        to your recipients also include your address and a Google Maps link with your
        coordinates, but not the full trail.
    </p>
    <p>
        The trail stays on your device until you delete the recording or the App, and
        stays in Google Drive until you delete it there. The App doesn't add your
        location to your video files. If you open a saved location in the App, it's
        sent to Google Maps.
    </p>

    <h2>Google Account Data</h2>
    <p>
        The App requires you to sign in with Google. Sign-in is handled by Google,
        and we never see your password. The App requests the following access:
    </p>
    <ul>
        <li>
            <strong>Email address (<code>userinfo.email</code>)</strong>: used to
            show which account is signed in. On iPhone, it can also be used to
            tell recipients who started recording.
        </li>
        <li>
            <strong>
                Name and profile photo, iPhone only (<code>userinfo.profile</code>)
            </strong>: used to show which account is signed in, and to tell
            recipients who started recording. The Android version doesn't request
            this access.
        </li>
        <li>
            <strong>
                Google Drive, limited to files the App creates or opens
                (<code>drive.file</code>)
            </strong>: used to create a folder for each recording, upload clips,
            a playlist file, and a location file if "Save location" is on, set the folder's sharing, download those files
            for playback, and show your Drive storage usage. The App can't see or
            change your other Drive files.
        </li>
        <li>
            <strong>Gmail, send only (<code>gmail.send</code>)</strong>: used to
            send notification and test emails from your account. The App can't
            read, change, or delete your email. Sent emails may appear in your
            Gmail Sent folder.
        </li>
    </ul>
    <p>
        The App's communication with Google takes place directly between your
        device and Google, over encrypted connections. We don't receive or store
        your Google data or sign-in tokens. Your tokens are stored on your device:
        on iPhone by Google's sign-in library, and on Android in the App's private
        storage.
    </p>
    <p>
        We use Google user data only to provide the App features described in this
        policy. We don't sell it, use it for advertising, transfer it to data
        brokers, or use it to develop, improve, or train generalized AI or machine
        learning models. No person at Just Free Software can read this data,
        because it never reaches us.
    </p>
    <p>
        Just Capture's use and transfer to any other app of information received
        from Google APIs will adhere to the{" "}
        <a href="https://developers.google.com/terms/api-services-user-data-policy">
            Google API Services User Data Policy
        </a>, including the Limited Use requirements.
    </p>

    <h2>Link Sharing and Who Can See Your Recordings</h2>
    <p>
        When you start a recording, the App creates a private folder in your Google
        Drive. If email notifications are on and you've added recipients, the App
        sets the folder to "Anyone with the link" with view-only access when it
        emails them. Clips in the folder inherit this setting, so recipients can
        watch without requesting access. <strong>If no email is sent about a
        recording, the App leaves its folder private.</strong>
    </p>
    <p>
        Once a folder is shared, anyone who has the link can view and download the
        recording and its location file, including
        people your recipients forward it to. The link doesn't expire. To stop link
        access, change the folder's sharing settings or delete it in Google Drive.
        This doesn't undo copies that someone has already downloaded.
    </p>
    <p>
        When you sign in, the App also creates a temporary folder with "sharing
        check" in its name, tries to share it by link, and then deletes it. This tells
        the App whether your account allows link sharing, so it can warn you if
        your recipients won't be able to open your videos.
    </p>

    <h2>Notification Emails</h2>
    <p>
        If you turn on email notifications and add recipients, the App sends them
        an email from your Gmail account when you start a recording. A second email
        may follow if the first was sent before the Drive link was ready, or if
        your Drive runs out of storage.
    </p>
    <p>
        Emails come from your Gmail address. Depending on your settings, they may
        include your subject and message, the recording's start time, your
        location, and the Drive link. On iPhone, the subject may also include your
        name or email address. Once sent, emails are under the control of the
        recipients and their email providers.
    </p>
    <p>
        Please make sure the people you add are happy to receive these emails.
    </p>

    <h2>Folders Shared With You</h2>
    <p>
        In the Shared tab on iPhone, or the Watch tab on Android, you can paste a
        link to a Drive folder that someone else shared. The App downloads its clips from Google to your phone for replay and
        saves the folder's name and ID on your device. These requests use the App's
        Google API key rather than your Google account. Google can see the request,
        including your device's network address.
    </p>

    <h2>Information Stored on Your Device</h2>
    <p>The App stores the following on your device:</p>
    <ul>
        <li>Your recorded clips, which stay on your phone after uploading</li>
        <li>Clips downloaded for replay</li>
        <li>
            Recording details, such as start times, locations, and Drive folder
            links
        </li>
        <li>Recipient email addresses, email subject and message</li>
        <li>Notification emails, including any location they contain</li>
        <li>Folders you've added to the Shared or Watch tab</li>
        <li>Your settings</li>
    </ul>
    <p>
        This information may be included in your iCloud or computer backups of your
        iPhone, or in your Android device backups, depending on your settings.
    </p>

    <h2>Third-Party Services</h2>
    <p>
        The App works with the services below. They handle information under their
        own privacy policies, and we aren't affiliated with them.
    </p>
    <ul>
        <li>
            <strong>Google</strong> (Sign-In, Drive, Gmail and, on Android, address
            lookup, Google Play, and Android):{" "}
            <a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy">Google Privacy Policy</a>
        </li>
        <li>
            <strong>Apple</strong> (on iPhone: address lookup through its maps
            service, App Store, and iOS):{" "}
            <a href="https://www.apple.com/legal/privacy/">Apple Privacy Policy</a>
        </li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Data Sharing and Sale</h2>
    <p>
        We don't sell, rent, or share your information, because it doesn't reach us.
        The App shares information only as described in this policy, in order to
        provide its features: with Google, with Apple on iPhone, with the recipients you choose,
        and with anyone who has the link to a shared recording.
    </p>

    <h2>Data Retention and Deletion</h2>
    <p>
        We don't keep your data on servers, so you control how long it's kept:
    </p>
    <ul>
        <li>
            <strong>On your phone</strong>: delete a recording in the App's My Clips
            tab to remove its clips and any pending uploads or emails. Removing a
            folder from the Shared or Watch tab deletes its downloaded clips. Uninstalling
            the App removes the App's data from your phone.
        </li>
        <li>
            <strong>In Google Drive</strong>: the App never deletes your uploaded
            clips, so deleting a recording in the App doesn't remove it from Drive.
            Delete it in Google Drive instead.
        </li>
        <li>
            <strong>In Gmail</strong>: you can delete sent emails from your account,
            but this doesn't remove them from your recipients' inboxes.
        </li>
        <li>
            <strong>Google access</strong>: signing out stops recording and pauses
            uploads and emails, but doesn't delete your clips or settings. To revoke
            the App's access, visit your{" "}
            <a href="https://myaccount.google.com/permissions">
                Google Account permissions
            </a>.
        </li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Security</h2>
    <p>
        The App connects to Google and, on iPhone, Apple over encrypted connections. No method
        of storage or transmission is completely secure. Your phone's passcode and
        your Google account's security settings also help protect your data.
    </p>

    <h2>Children's Privacy</h2>
    <p>
        The App isn't directed to children under 13, and we don't knowingly collect
        personal information from them.
    </p>

    <h2>Changes to This Privacy Policy</h2>
    <p>
        We may update this Privacy Policy when the App's functionality or data
        practices change. Any updated version will be posted at this location with a
        new "Last updated" date.
    </p>

    <h2>Contact</h2>
    <p>
        If you have questions about this Privacy Policy or Just Capture's privacy
        practices, please contact us at:{" "}
        <a href="mailto:justfreesoftwarema@gmail.com">
            justfreesoftwarema@gmail.com
        </a>
    </p>
</Layout>
